From 702ff37ab97d207fb6866f7b62ef2dc0936455cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:41:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WAM: give exhibition (dock) mode windows a window type of
 their own

Exhibition mode - the display a device shows while it sits in a charging
dock - hosts an application full screen. The shell launches it with the
parameters legacy webOS used, { "windowType": "dockModeWindow",
"dockMode": true }, which the ported applications still look for to pick
their dock face (com.palm.app.photos' PhotoAppLauncher::appSelect
switches to its slideshow face on exactly that, and com.palm.app.clock
documents the same contract).

Until now such a window came up as an ordinary card, so a docked
application also sat in the card stack behind the exhibition display.
Honour those launch parameters with _WEBOS_WINDOW_TYPE_DOCK so the shell
can host it apart from the cards, and accept "dock" in
WindowTypeFromString so an application can also declare it through
appinfo.json's defaultWindowType.

A dock window is an ordinary full-screen webOS window, so the Luna app
factory builds it as a WebAppWaylandWebOS alongside the card and system
UI types; without that it would reach the factory only to be turned away
as BAD_WINDOW_TYPE.

The applications this is for are typically "noWindow": true - they open
the window the user actually sees through window.open - so that child
has to carry the type as well. It was taking it from appinfo.json's
defaultWindowType, which knows nothing about how this launch was asked
for, and so fell back to a card. Inherit the type the parent was created
with when there is one, and keep the appinfo default as the fallback.
Upstream-Status: Pending

